18. IPFS CONTENT ADDRESSING
==================================================

Each published GKS snapshot has a root CID.

EXAMPLE:

mathematics.gks -> CID_A
programming.gks -> CID_B
physics.gks     -> CID_C

CATALOGUE RECORD:

ARCHIVE_NAME
ROOT_CID
SNAPSHOT_VERSION
SCHEMA_VERSION
INDEX_CIDS
DEPENDENCY_REFERENCES
PUBLISHER_IDENTITY
SIGNATURE
AVAILABILITY_METADATA

Updated snapshots receive new root CIDs.

Logical archive names can resolve through
signed manifests or IPNS.

GammaThink object IDs identify canonical
knowledge objects.

IPFS CIDs identify stored content blocks.

An index maps knowledge object IDs to
their containing IPFS blocks.

CID integrity proves content identity,
not factual correctness.


